is fixed or liquidated or is capable of being ascertained by fixed rules or as a matter of opinion, including any liability under any
enactment (in England and Wales or in any other jurisdiction) and any liability in contract, tort or bailment or arising out of an obligation
to make restitution or in any other manner. For the avoidance of doubt, where any contract is void or, being voidable, has been duly
avoided, no obligation or liability shall arise in respect of such contract and to the extent that it does, it shall constitute a Liability
for the purposes of this definition.</P>

